// due: a timer park has no lowering in the coroutine slice yet
// refuses: coro.not-yet at 13:5
// `yield_now` and `sleep` park through `std.task`'s park points, whose
// panicking bodies stand in for the lowering coroutines bring. A park point
// is summarized from its lang role as declared-suspending, so a call to one
// suspends whatever that body holds. The ready park under `yield_now` is
// lowered and the timer park under `sleep` is not, so `main`'s frame is
// refused at the `sleep` call, rather than built into a call of the body.
import std.task.{yield_now}

func main() {
    yield_now()
    sleep(Duration.ms(1))
    print("{}", 1)
}
